Bash Notes
Conditionals
---------------

In an if statement you can echo with either double quotes (""), single quotes (''), or no quotes at all.
Double quotes will allow for variable expansion.
Signle quotes will not allow varibale expansion.

Use 'help test' to figure out what bash can test for.
Use 'run-help' in place of 'help' for ZSH.

"true" and "false" are commands.

You can use conditionals as normal commands and even chain them:
[[ -f file.txt ]] && echo it exists!

